5194: # ----------------------------------------------------------------------------- task lock + pending record
5195: #
5196: # OWNERSHIP and RECOVERY METADATA are two different files:
5197: #
5198: #   <task>/.consult.lock          ownership. A PERMANENT file at a stable path: opened
5199: #                                 with FileMode.OpenOrCreate and held open for the whole
5200: #                                 critical section; release = close the handle, never
5201: #                                 unlink (a contender that already opened the path must
5202: #                                 never end up locking a different file than the next
5203: #                                 one). The OS decides ownership: a holder that dies
5204: #                                 loses it with its handle. Share mode:
5205: #                                   * Windows: FileShare.Read - a refused contender can
5206: #                                     read the holder's record for its message, nobody
5207: #                                     else can open it for writing;
5208: #                                   * elsewhere: FileShare.None, which .NET on Unix
5209: #                                     emulates with an advisory flock(LOCK_EX) (any other
5210: #                                     share mode maps to a shared lock that would not
5211: #                                     exclude).
5212: #                                 Cross-host exclusion (a task directory on a network
5213: #                                 share used from two machines) is out of scope. The
5214: #                                 content is informational only - { pid, start_time,
5215: #                                 host, task, started } of the current holder, plus
5216: #                                 `panel` (its id) while a -Panel run holds it - written
5217: #                                 after the handle is held; overwriting it destroys
5218: #                                 nothing recoverable. A -Panel run holds it for the
5219: #                                 whole panel; its members never take it.
5220: #
5221: #   <task>/.consult.write.lock    (0.4.x wave 21) the COMMIT lock of the task's two stores,
5222: #                                 same discipline (permanent file, held open, release =
5223: #                                 close, a killed holder releases it), held only for one
5224: #                                 commit and waited for (Enter-WriteLock: backoff up to
5225: #                                 60 s). Every writer of findings.json / sessions.json -
5226: #                                 a single run, a panel member, codex-findings.ps1 -Status
5227: #                                 and -Rate - goes through Enter-StoreCommit: lock,
5228: #                                 RE-READ both stores, apply its own delta, write, release.
5229: #                                 No writer ever writes a store snapshot read before it.

1: <#
2: .SYNOPSIS
3:     Usefulness telemetry: which reviewer was useful on which kind of question.
4: 
5: .DESCRIPTION
6:     Reads the ledgers (<CollabDir>/<task>/sessions.json) and findings stores
7:     (<CollabDir>/<task>/findings.json) of EVERY task of this repository, or of one task
8:     with -Task, and prints one row per (reviewer lineage, purpose), a total row per
9:     lineage and a grand total. Nothing is written, no lock is taken; a store that cannot
10:     be read is reported and left out. Exit 0.
11: 
12:     Row key
13:       REVIEWER   '<provider> :: <model>' of the consultation (its ledger reviewer), with
14:                  ' [<engine>]' appended for an engine other than codex (0.4.0, e.g.
15:                  'gemini :: gemini-3.8-flash-high [agy]'; an absent reviewer.engine is
16:                  codex); 'unknown provenance' for entries recorded before 0.3.0 (no reviewer)
17:       PURPOSE    the consultation's purpose, '(none)' without one; '(total)' on a
18:                  lineage's total row; the grand total row is '(all) (total)'
19:     Columns (JSON field in brackets)
20:       CONSULTS   ledger entries [consults]
21:       USABLE     bridge_outcome 'usable reply' [usable]
22:       PROSE      usable, but no valid structured reply (-Raw, chore, invalid JSON) [prose]
23:       FAILED     every other outcome [failed]
24:       RAISED     findings raised by these consultations (a finding belongs to the
25:                  consultation it was ingested from: source.consult = the entry's n, in
26:                  the same task - the join codex-findings.ps1 -Stats uses) [raised]
27:       VERIFIED / REJECTED / WONTFIX / SUPERSEDED   their current status [verified,
28:                  rejected, wontfix, superseded]
29:       OPEN       proposed + implemented [open]
30:       HIT%       verified / (verified + rejected), rounded percent; '-' when both are 0
31:                  [hit_rate: a number, or null]
32:       A/H/R/D    verdicts ACCEPT / HOLD / REJECT / ADVISE [verdict_accept, verdict_hold,
33:                  verdict_reject, verdict_advise]
34:       Y/P/N      the judge's usefulness marks (codex-findings.ps1 -Rate): yes / partly /
35:                  no [rated_yes, rated_partly, rated_no]
36:       MEDIAN_S   median wall_seconds; '-' when none [median_wall_seconds: number or null]
37:       TOKENS     input tokens not served from the cache / output tokens [tokens_in,
38:                  tokens_out]
39:     Findings whose consultation has no ledger entry count as 'unknown provenance' /
40:     '(none)'. Rows are sorted by lineage (case-insensitive; unknown provenance last),
41:     then purpose. -Json prints an array of the same rows with numeric fields (plus
42:     `kind`: purpose | lineage | total).
43: 
44: .EXAMPLE
45:     powershell -NoProfile -ExecutionPolicy Bypass -File codex-scoreboard.ps1
46: 
47: .EXAMPLE
48:     pwsh -NoProfile -File codex-scoreboard.ps1 -Task cache-rewrite -Json
49: #>
50: [CmdletBinding()]
51: param(
52:     # Where consultations are stored. Relative paths resolve against the git repo root.
53:     [string]$CollabDir = '.collab',
54: 
55:     # One task only (its directory under <CollabDir>).
56:     [string]$Task = '',
57: 
58:     # An array of row objects instead of the table.
59:     [switch]$Json
60: )
61: 
62: $ErrorActionPreference = 'Stop'
63: $script:ToolName = 'codex-scoreboard'
64: . (Join-Path $PSScriptRoot 'codex-consult-common.ps1')
65: 
66: if ($Task -and $Task -notmatch '^[A-Za-z0-9][A-Za-z0-9._-]*$') {
67:     Stop-WithError "-Task must be a slug (letters, digits, dot, dash, underscore)."
68: }
69: $repoRoot = Resolve-RepoRoot -Cwd (Get-Location).Path
70: $collabRoot = Resolve-CollabRoot -RepoRoot $repoRoot -CollabDir $CollabDir
71: 
72: $taskDirs = @()
73: if ($Task) {
74:     $one = Join-Path $collabRoot $Task
75:     if (-not (Test-Path -LiteralPath $one -PathType Container)) { Stop-WithError "no task '$Task' under $collabRoot." }
76:     $taskDirs = @(Get-Item -LiteralPath $one)
77: } elseif (Test-Path -LiteralPath $collabRoot -PathType Container) {
78:     $taskDirs = @(Get-ChildItem -LiteralPath $collabRoot -Directory | Sort-Object Name)
79: }
80: 
81: # Tolerant reads: a store that does not parse is reported and left out.
82: $notes = New-Object System.Collections.Generic.List[string]
83: function Read-TolerantStore {
84:     param([string]$Path)
85:     if (-not (Test-Path -LiteralPath $Path -PathType Leaf)) { return $null }
86:     try { return (ConvertFrom-JsonKeepOffset -Text (Read-SharedText -Path $Path)) } catch {
87:         $notes.Add("left out: $Path does not parse ($(ConvertTo-OneLine $_.Exception.Message))")
88:         return $null
89:     }
90: }
91: 
92: function Get-IntValue {
93:     param($Object, [string]$Name)
94:     $v = Get-PropertyValue $Object $Name $null
95:     $n = [long]0
96:     if ($null -ne $v -and [long]::TryParse([string]$v, [ref]$n)) { return $n }
97:     return $null
98: }
99: 
100: # One accumulator per row key.
101: $rows = @{}
102: function Get-Acc {
103:     param([string]$Lineage, [string]$Purpose)
104:     $key = "$Lineage`t$Purpose"
105:     if (-not $rows.ContainsKey($key)) {
106:         $rows[$key] = [pscustomobject]@{
107:             Lineage = $Lineage; Purpose = $Purpose; Consults = 0; Usable = 0; Prose = 0; Failed = 0
108:             Raised = 0; Verified = 0; Rejected = 0; Wontfix = 0; Superseded = 0; Open = 0
109:             Accept = 0; Hold = 0; Reject = 0; Advise = 0; Yes = 0; Partly = 0; No = 0
110:             Walls = (New-Object System.Collections.Generic.List[double]); TokensIn = [long]0; TokensOut = [long]0
111:         }
112:     }
113:     return $rows[$key]
114: }
115: 
116: foreach ($dir in $taskDirs) {
117:     $sessions = Read-TolerantStore -Path (Join-Path $dir.FullName 'sessions.json')
118:     $store = Read-TolerantStore -Path (Join-Path $dir.FullName 'findings.json')
119:     $keyOf = @{}
120:     foreach ($c in @(Get-PropertyValue (Get-PropertyValue $sessions 'codex' $null) 'consults' @())) {
121:         if ($null -eq $c) { continue }
122:         $rev = Get-PropertyValue $c 'reviewer' $null
123:         $lineage = 'unknown provenance'
124:         if ($null -ne $rev) { $lineage = Format-ReviewerLineage -Provider ([string](Get-PropertyValue $rev 'provider' '')) -Model ([string](Get-PropertyValue $rev 'model' '')) -Engine ([string](Get-PropertyValue $rev 'engine' '')) }
125:         $purpose = [string](Get-PropertyValue $c 'purpose' '')
126:         if (-not $purpose) { $purpose = '(none)' }
127:         $acc = Get-Acc $lineage $purpose
128:         $n = Get-IntValue $c 'n'
129:         if ($null -ne $n) { $keyOf[$n] = $acc }
130:         $acc.Consults++
131:         $outcome = [string](Get-PropertyValue $c 'bridge_outcome' (Get-PropertyValue $c 'outcome' ''))
132:         if ($outcome -eq 'usable reply') {
133:             $acc.Usable++
134:             if ((Get-PropertyValue $c 'structured' $false) -ne $true) { $acc.Prose++ }
135:         } else {
136:             $acc.Failed++
137:         }
138:         switch ([string](Get-PropertyValue $c 'verdict' '')) {
139:             'ACCEPT' { $acc.Accept++ }
140:             'HOLD' { $acc.Hold++ }
141:             'REJECT' { $acc.Reject++ }
142:             'ADVISE' { $acc.Advise++ }
143:         }
144:         $wall = Get-PropertyValue $c 'wall_seconds' $null
145:         $w = [double]0
146:         if ($null -ne $wall -and [double]::TryParse([string]$wall, [System.Globalization.NumberStyles]::Float, $script:Invariant, [ref]$w)) { $acc.Walls.Add($w) }
147:         $usage = Get-PropertyValue $c 'usage' $null
148:         if ($null -ne $usage) {
149:             $in = Get-IntValue $usage 'input_tokens'
150:             $cached = Get-IntValue $usage 'cached_input_tokens'
151:             $out = Get-IntValue $usage 'output_tokens'
152:             if ($null -ne $in) { $acc.TokensIn += [Math]::Max([long]0, $in - $(if ($null -ne $cached) { $cached } else { 0 })) }
153:             if ($null -ne $out) { $acc.TokensOut += $out }
154:         }
155:     }
156:     foreach ($f in @(Get-PropertyValue $store 'findings' @())) {
157:         if ($null -eq $f) { continue }
158:         $n = Get-IntValue (Get-PropertyValue $f 'source' $null) 'consult'
159:         $acc = $null
160:         if ($null -ne $n -and $keyOf.ContainsKey($n)) { $acc = $keyOf[$n] } else { $acc = Get-Acc 'unknown provenance' '(none)' }
161:         $acc.Raised++
162:         switch ([string](Get-PropertyValue $f 'status' '')) {
163:             'verified' { $acc.Verified++ }
164:             'rejected' { $acc.Rejected++ }
165:             'wontfix' { $acc.Wontfix++ }
166:             'superseded' { $acc.Superseded++ }
167:             'proposed' { $acc.Open++ }
168:             'implemented' { $acc.Open++ }
169:         }
170:     }
171:     foreach ($rt in @(Get-PropertyValue $store 'ratings' @())) {
172:         if ($null -eq $rt) { continue }
173:         $n = Get-IntValue $rt 'n'
174:         $acc = $null
175:         if ($null -ne $n -and $keyOf.ContainsKey($n)) { $acc = $keyOf[$n] }
176:         else {
177:             $p = [string](Get-PropertyValue $rt 'purpose' '')
178:             $acc = Get-Acc ([string](Get-PropertyValue $rt 'lineage' 'unknown provenance')) $(if ($p) { $p } else { '(none)' })
179:         }
180:         switch ([string](Get-PropertyValue $rt 'useful' '')) {
181:             'yes' { $acc.Yes++ }
182:             'partly' { $acc.Partly++ }
183:             'no' { $acc.No++ }
184:         }
185:     }
186: }
