1024: # ----------------------------------------------------------------------------- review panel (-Panel)
1025: #
1026: # The roster is walked like the single-reviewer walk, without stopping at the first available
1027: # entry (Select-PanelMembers). Each member then runs as a complete consultation of its own - a
1028: # child run of this script (-PanelSpec) in a process of its own: own preflight, own recovery
1029: # record .consult.pending-<NN>.json, own parent thread (the newest of its lineage, or a new one;
1030: # -Mode new: new for all), own consultation id, handoff files
1031: # handoffs/NN-<engine>-<ReplyName>-<provider>.md and ledger entry with the `panel` record.
1032: # 0.4.x wave 21 (ROADMAP R11) - the members run IN PARALLEL; this run:
1033: #   1. takes the task lock (.consult.lock; its informational record names the panel) and holds
1034: #      it until the summary is printed: no other consultation or status update of the task in
1035: #      between (D12);
1036: #   2. judges EVERY recovery record of the task first: an active one refuses the panel, the
1037: #      inactive ones are consumed (numbering skips past them; D5);
1038: #   3. assigns n and NN to every member up front, in roster order (member k: n0 + k - 1,
1039: #      NN0 + k - 1), so the files and the ledger keep the roster order whatever finishes first;
1040: #   4. writes every member's `reserved` record (the panel, n, NN, this process as writer and
1041: #      parent) BEFORE it launches any member - a member proves its parent with it, rewrites it
1042: #      with its own pid and only then checks that the parent lives (D6, D1, F07-1);
1043: #   5. launches the members as processes of their own (Start-Process; console output to files
1044: #      in a temp directory) along the plan of Get-PanelPlan - members of different endpoints at
1045: #      once, of one endpoint one after another unless the roster's "parallel" raises it,
1046: #      -PanelConcurrency caps the total (D8) - polls them, prints one line per finished member
1047: #      and stops a member that outlives its guard (its timeout + its format-repair and
1048: #      denial-retry budgets + 60 s write lock + 120 s, D11);
1049: #   6. prints every member's console output in roster order, the summary with the panel's wall
1050: #      clock, and removes the records of members that never started anything (D5).
1051: # A member that fails or is refused does not stop the others; with -PanelConcurrency 1 a member
1052: # that leaves surviving processes stops the rest (recorded as skipped, exit 1; F15-3). Exit 0
1053: # only when every member produced a usable reply (-DryRun: when every member's plan could be
1054: # made; a dry run writes nothing and takes no lock).
1055: 
1056: # The ledger entry a panel member recorded (the task's sessions.json, read tolerantly).
1057: function Find-PanelEntry {
1058:     param([string]$Path, [string]$PanelId, [int]$Position)
1059:     if (-not (Test-Path -LiteralPath $Path -PathType Leaf)) { return $null }
1060:     $data = $null
1061:     try { $data = ConvertFrom-Json -InputObject (Read-SharedText -Path $Path) } catch { return $null }
1062:     $found = $null
1063:     foreach ($c in @(Get-PropertyValue (Get-PropertyValue $data 'codex' $null) 'consults' @())) {
1064:         $pr = Get-PropertyValue $c 'panel' $null
1065:         if ($null -ne $pr -and [string](Get-PropertyValue $pr 'id' '') -eq $PanelId -and [string](Get-PropertyValue $pr 'position' '') -eq [string]$Position) { $found = $c }
1066:     }
1067:     return $found
1068: }
